	)
	(text "NOTE #1: USB CONNECTION OPERATES USING USB 2.0 ON-THE-GO (OTG). THIS PROVIDES POWER TO\nTHE MCU VIA VBUS--REGULATED DOWN TO 3.3V (NOMINAL) BEFORE ENTERING THE STM32. D- AND\nD+ LINES ARE DIFFERENTIAL PAIRS. CC1 AND CC2 ARE PULLED-DOWN WITH 5.1k RESISTORS PER \nTHE USB SPECIFICATION. SBU1, SBU2 ARE PINS IMPLEMENTED IN THE USB-C STANDARD; HOWEVER, \nTHEY ARE NOT NEEDED FOR USB 2.0 OTG, SO THEY ARE LEFT FLOATING. THE ID PIN ON THE STM32\nIS LEFT FLOATING--PER THE OTG STANDARD, THIS SHOULD CAUSE THE STM32 TO ACT AS A DEVICE\nRATHER THAN AS A HOST."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 59.69 338.074 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 0 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "b5fdade8-6e89-4492-a1de-2036276912e1")
	)
